# Dynamic Media design system

This project follows the Dynamic Media internal-app design system
(originating in the Sales Research Engine). When building UI, follow
these conventions exactly — do not invent parallel treatments.

## Color and theming

- Brand accent is `#00AEEF` (Dynamic Media cyan). It is exposed ONLY
  through the `accent` token. Never hard-code hex values in components.
- All colors come from the semantic Tailwind classes wired in
  `tailwind.config.ts` → CSS variables in `app/globals.css`:
  - `bg-surface-primary` (page bg), `bg-surface-secondary` (cards,
    sidebar, topbar), `bg-surface-elevated` (hovers, wells),
    `border-surface-border` / `ring-surface-border` (hairlines)
  - `text-text-primary`, `text-text-secondary`, `text-text-muted`
  - `bg-accent`, `hover:bg-accent-hover`, `bg-accent-muted`
- Dark mode is class-based (`next-themes`, `.dark` on `<html>`), dark
  by default. Because everything reads tokens, components need no
  `dark:` variants for the core palette — only for one-off tinted
  states (e.g. `dark:bg-rose-900/40`).

## Layout shell

- Fixed 240px (`w-60`) sidebar on the left with the DM logo header
  (white-blue lockup in dark mode, black-blue in light), grouped nav
  sections with 10px uppercase tracked labels, and a quiet footer.
- Fixed 56px (`h-14`) top bar with theme toggle and avatar menu.
- Main content: `ml-60 pt-20 px-8 pb-8 bg-surface-primary`.
- Pages with chrome live inside the `(shell)` route group; chrome-free
  pages (sign-in, print views) live outside it.
- Nav links use `.sidebar-link` / `.sidebar-link-active` from
  globals.css; a primary "start here" CTA uses `.sidebar-link-primary`.

## Primitives — use these, don't re-derive

- `components/ui/Card.tsx` — the ONE surface container: `rounded-xl`,
  solid `surface-secondary`, single `ring-1` hairline, `p-5`. Tones for
  accent/warning/success; optional colored left accent bar.
- `components/ui/SectionHeader.tsx` — the ONE section header: thin
  uppercase tracked label + small lucide icon + optional right action.
  Icon and label share one accent color per section.
- `components/ui/GroupLabel.tsx` — labeled hairline divider naming a
  zone of cards; one tier above SectionHeader.
- `components/ui/Badge.tsx` — the ONE pill/chip: semantic `tone` for
  status/severity, `tone="none"` + className for identity palettes.
- `components/ui/DataTable.tsx` — dense table shell (`text-xs`,
  hairline dividers, subtle hover). Use the exported row/cell class
  constants; numeric columns add `tabular-nums`.
- `components/ui/EmptySectionCard.tsx` — the ONE empty-state: accent
  bar card + header + full-width dashed CTA styled with
  `emptySectionCtaClass`.

## Buttons and inputs

There is deliberately no `<Button>` component. Use the canonical class
recipes (see `app/(shell)/styleguide/InteractiveDemos.tsx`):

- Primary: `bg-accent … hover:bg-accent-hover` (h-9, rounded-md, sm text)
- Secondary: bordered `bg-surface-elevated`
- Danger: `bg-red-600 hover:bg-red-500`
- Inputs: `rounded-md border border-surface-border bg-surface-primary
  px-3 py-2 text-sm … focus:border-accent focus:ring-1 focus:ring-accent`

## Dialogs and notifications

- Native `window.confirm` / `alert` / `prompt` are BANNED (enforced in
  `.eslintrc.json`). Never use them.
- Yes/no questions: `useConfirm()` from `components/ConfirmDialog.tsx`
  (promise-based; `tone: "danger"` for destructive actions).
- Transient notifications: `react-hot-toast` (`toast.success`,
  `toast.error`) — the Toaster is already styled with surface tokens.
- Anything needing input: a purpose-built portal modal styled like the
  ConfirmDialog (border-surface-border, bg-surface-secondary,
  shadow-2xl, accent top border).

## Iconography and type

- Icons: lucide-react only, `strokeWidth={1.8}`. Sizes: 18 in nav,
  13 in section headers, 14–16 in buttons/menus.
- Font: Inter via `next/font` (`--font-inter`), weights 300–700.
- Type scale: `text-2xl font-semibold` page titles, `text-base
  font-semibold` dialog headings, `text-sm` body, `text-xs` metadata,
  10–11px uppercase tracked labels.
